  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set that maps the customer's regression to the actual stage boundary:\n\n**Babel side** (`packages/babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts`) \u2014 the legacy vs. stage-3 fork: `legacy: true` or `version: \"legacy\"` routes to `transformer-legacy.ts` (the Reflect-metadata-compatible, TS `experimentalDecorators`-style transform); any other version routes to `createClassFeaturePlugin` with the TC39 stage-3 semantics, which has no metadata-emission hook at all. `packages/babel-plugin-transform-typescript/src/index.ts` shows Babel's TS plugin only strips types/handles class-field stripping \u2014 it never emits `design:paramtypes`/`Reflect.metadata` itself, so metadata only survives if the legacy decorators plugin runs and Nest's `Reflect.metadata()` call sites are left in place.\n\n**SWC side** (`crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs`, `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_typescript/src/typescript.rs`, `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/mod.rs`, `decorator_2022_03.rs`) \u2014 `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator` and `jsc.transform.decoratorMetadata` are two independent booleans wired together in `config/mod.rs`: `legacy_decorator` selects between `swc_ecma_transforms_proposal::decorators` (legacy) and `decorator_2022_03` (stage-3), while `decorator_metadata` (`emit_metadata`) is passed separately into `swc_ecma_transforms_typescript::typescript()`, which is what actually emits the `_ts_metadata(\"design:paramtypes\", \u2026)` helper calls (per `bindings/binding_core_wasm/src/types.rs` docs referencing `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator`/`decoratorMetadata`).\n\nThe divergence: SWC's metadata emission is gated on **decoratorMetadata alone being true**, independent of legacyDecorator \u2014 but decorator *metadata* is only meaningful with the legacy/experimental form. If the customer's `.swcrc` has `legacyDecorator: false` (or omitted, default `false`) with `decoratorMetadata` true or false, SWC either emits stage-3 decorators (no metadata concept exists there) or emits legacy decorators without the `_ts_metadata` calls \u2014 either way Nest's `Reflect.getMetadata` lookups come back `undefined`. The fix is setting both `legacyDecorator: true` **and** `decoratorMetadata: true` together in `jsc.transform`, mirroring the paired Babel config of `@babel/plugin-proposal-decorators` with `legacy: true` alongside `@babel/plugin-transform-typescript`.",
